-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 71: add `source.processing_stage` — the per-source pipeline status
--   (Track PL.2).
--
-- WHY. Track PL makes ingest auto-chain `parse -> embed -> EXTRACT (-> GRAPH ->
-- INSIGHTS)`. Today nothing on the source row records HOW FAR a document has
-- progressed, so the UI cannot show per-document progress and the pipeline
-- cannot be resumed from where it stopped. `processing_stage` is that visible,
-- resumable status. PL.2 writes `ingested -> embedded -> extracted`
-- (+ `awaiting_schema_review` when the schema-review gate parks extraction,
-- `failed` on a hard error); PL.3/PL.4 add `graphed`/`complete`.
--
-- FIELD SHAPE. A plain strict `string` (not `option<>`) DEFAULT "ingested":
-- every source has a definite stage — there is no honest "NONE / no stage"
-- value (a freshly created row IS at least `ingested`), so a strict string with
-- a default is the right model and keeps reads/writes simple (no option-unwrap
-- in the handler transitions). The accepted values are an app-level enum
-- (ingested | embedded | extracted | awaiting_schema_review | graphed |
-- complete | failed); SurrealDB stores the bare string. Idempotent: a handler
-- re-running a stage just re-writes the same value.
--
-- S.4 RULE (strict field on an EXISTING SCHEMAFULL table -> MUST backfill).
-- The `source` table is SCHEMAFULL (migration 1) and already holds rows. A
-- SurrealDB SCHEMAFULL table re-validates the WHOLE record on any UPDATE; a
-- DEFAULT applies only to rows created AFTER this migration, so pre-existing
-- rows would keep NONE in the new strict field and the strict type would then
-- silently block ALL future writes to those rows ("Found NONE for field
-- processing_stage, expected a string"). Per migrations/README.md and the S.2
-- forward-guard (migration 65 `source.private`), we backfill in the SAME
-- migration with a DRIFT-ONLY `WHERE processing_stage = NONE` so a healthy DB
-- matches 0 rows (true no-op, startup-safe) and only genuinely-NONE rows are
-- touched.
--
-- BACKFILL VALUE. Existing sources predate the pipeline-stage model; they were
-- ingested (and most were embedded) before this field existed. We backfill the
-- conservative `"ingested"` rather than guessing `embedded`/`extracted`: the
-- pipeline is idempotent and resumable, so a re-run from `ingested` re-embeds
-- (idempotent: embed deletes-then-writes) and re-extracts (idempotent: dedups
-- per (in,out,type)) without corruption. A staging backfill of the true stage
-- for the live corpus, if desired, is a separate gated data task — not this
-- schema migration.
--
-- Idempotent + forward-only. Re-running DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE re-asserts the
-- identical definition; the drift-only UPDATE matches nothing on a second pass.
-- Down removes the field (faithful inverse: the field is brand new here).
-- ============================================================================

-- 1. Declare the strict field with a default. Applies to rows created from now
--    on; pre-existing rows are handled by the backfill below.
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE processing_stage ON TABLE source TYPE string DEFAULT "ingested";

-- 2. S.4 backfill — drift-only WHERE so a healthy DB matches 0 rows (no rewrite,
--    startup-safe) and only pre-existing NONE rows are repaired. Mirrors
--    migration 65's `source.private` coalesce shape exactly.
UPDATE source SET
    processing_stage = processing_stage ?? "ingested"
    WHERE processing_stage = NONE
    RETURN NONE;
